;; review4 bug-11 (P3, error text): encoding/json names the failing value's
;; position in an out-of-range number error ("into .0 of type float64" for
;; array index 0); the natives.lg read-json twin always says "into Go value".
;; Since let-go ff1e6da (let-go#995, D198) every out-of-range number here reads
;; "json: number 1e400 out of range" (no path); the lines below are 4e769212's.
;; native lg 4e769212 prints:
;; json: cannot unmarshal number 1e400 into .0 of type float64
;; json: cannot unmarshal number 1e400 into Go value of type float64
(println (try (json/read-json "[1e400]") (catch Exception e (ex-message e))))
(println (try (json/read-json "1e400") (catch Exception e (ex-message e))))
